<h1><span lang="EN-GB">Merge</span></h1>
<hr align="left" width="98.974%" size="6" class="whs3">
<p>This command is accessible from <span class="Path" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Scan Data &gt; Merge</b></span>.</p>
<p class="Description"><span lang="EN-US" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Description:</b></span> <span class="Command">Merge</span> <span lang="EN-GB">command</span> creates a single polygon mesh from visible and selected scan data and mesh entities. <span lang="EN-GB">It is one of the most important operations in KUBE. Merge dramatically reduces dataset noise without reducing accuracy.</span></p>
<p class="Normal" style="text-align:justify;"><span lang="EN-GB"><img src="../Mesh/images/merge.gif" width="446px" height="131px" border="0" class="img_whs4" alt="">&#160;</span></p>
<p class="parameterstitle"><span lang="EN-GB">Sensor type</span></p>
<p class="parameterdescription"><span lang="EN-GB">Select the sensor type. KUBE software uses the currently detected sensor. If no sensor is attached 'Unknown' profile is used. The default values are set based on this information. Select 'Custom' if you do not want to use recommended values for Merge.</span></p>
<p class="parameterstitle"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Point spacing</b></span></p>
<p class="parameterdescription"><span lang="EN-GB">The lower bound for distance between points.</span></p>
<p class="parameterstitle"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Advanced &gt;&gt;</b></span></p>
<p class="Normal" style="text-align:justify;"><img src="../Mesh/images/merge_2.gif" width="446px" height="183px" border="0" class="img_whs5" alt=""><br>
When only scan data or both scan data and meshes are selected</p>
<p class="Normal" style="text-align:justify;"><img src="../Mesh/images/merge_3.gif" width="446px" height="183px" border="0" class="img_whs5" alt=""><br>
When only meshes are selected</p>
<p class="parameterstitle"><span lang="EN-GB">Advanced - Before Merge</span></p>
<ul class="whs6">
<li style="text-align:justify;" class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Area sampling</b></span> <span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>UV</b></span> <span lang="EN-GB">- &#160;if checked, applies <a href="area_2d_sampling.htm">2D sampling</a> prior to merge. This option is applicable to scan data only.</span></p>
</li>
<li style="text-align:justify;" class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Optimise scan</b></span> <span lang="EN-GB">– if checked, applies optimisation prior to merge. This option is applicable to both scan data and meshes.</span> <span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b><a href="Optimise_Scan.htm">Optimise Scan</a></b></span> <span lang="EN-GB">is applied to selected scan data and <a href="Optimise_Meshes.htm">Optimise Meshes</a> is applied to selected meshes. Default value for optimisation is 1mm.</span></p>
</li>
<li style="text-align:justify;" class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Sample 1 in every</b></span> <span lang="EN-GB">- sets value for sampling during scan data optimisation. This option is not visible when scan optimising is disabled. If enabled the default sampling value is 2 points.</span></p>
</li>
</ul>
<p class="parameterstitle"><span lang="EN-GB">Advanced - After Merge</span></p>
<ul class="whs6">
<li style="text-align:justify;" class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>3D polygon reduction</b></span> <span lang="EN-GB">– if checked, applies <a href="Polygon_Reduction.htm">3D polygon reduction</a> after merge.</span></p>
</li>
<li style="text-align:justify;" class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Insert Boundary points</b></span> <span lang="EN-GB">- in cases when area sampling is applied before merge, part of the scan data boundary points will be lost and the boundary of the result mesh will differ from the original one. If the option is enabled, all boundary points will be kept and the result mesh will have exactly the same shape as the scan data. Unchecked by default.</span></p>
</li>
<li style="text-align:justify;" class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Curvature Analysis</b></span> <span lang="EN-GB">- analyses the curvature of the data and enhances the detected edges.</span></p>
</li>
</ul>
<p><span lang="EN-GB">This command is grayed if there is no selection or all selections are hidden. It works on entire entity, no matter if the scans or meshes are selected wholly or partially. Note that if you have selected several scan data entities, all of them will be merged into a single mesh entity.</span></p>
<p><span lang="EN-GB">The merge is very complicated process and on some large scans it may take long time to complete. The space occupied by the data is divided into many small cubes or <b><a class="expandspot" href="javascript:kadovTextPopup(this)" id="a2" style="font-weight:normal;">voxels</a> <span class="expandtext" style="display:'none';" id="POPUP170311315"><span lang="EN-GB">.<br>
<img src="../mesh/commands_files/image379.gif" width="490px" height="181px" border="0" class="img_whs7" alt=""><br>
&#160;</span></span></b>. The data patches are then loaded into the 3D grid, i.e. the grid is populated. The implicit surface is calculated and finally a new set of polygons representing the surface is generated.</span></p>
<p class="Example" style="text-decoration:underline;"><span lang="EN-GB"><a class="dropspot" href="javascript:kadovTextPopup(this)" id="a3" style="text-decoration:underline;">Examples</a></span></p>
<div class="droptext" id="POPUP171339873" style="display:'none'; x-ss-type:dropdown;">
